=product @PRODUCER@ @BASE@ VMSCURL @PCSIVERSION@ full
1 'PRODUCER
=prompt @PRODUCER@
1 'PRODUCT
=prompt curl @VERSION@ for OpenVMS (vms-curl)
1 'NOTICE
=prompt curl is distributed under the curl licence (MIT style).
1 RELEASE_NOTES
=prompt Documentation is in [VMSCURL.DOC]README.VMS under the installation directory.
1 POST_INSTALL
=prompt Post-installation tasks for curl (vms-curl)
    At system startup: to define VMSCURL$ROOT at every boot, add this line
    to SYS$MANAGER:SYSTARTUP_VMS.COM:
    $ @SYS$STARTUP:VMSCURL$STARTUP.COM
    For each user: to define the curl command, add this line to LOGIN.COM
    (or SYLOGIN.COM, for everyone):
    $ @VMSCURL$ROOT:[000000]VMSCURL$SETUP.COM
    In batch jobs, quote options that use capital letters ("-F") or use
    SET PROCESS/PARSE_STYLE=EXTENDED first.

PRODUCT REMOVE VMSCURL removes the product and deassigns VMSCURL$ROOT.
